+**Informative, unadopted billboard wire proposal (CX-020):** This provisional
+profile preserves the six semantic fields; issuer and signature are envelope
+metadata. It changes no existing core policy or protocol requirement.
+
+- `RPPB` magic, version byte 1, kind byte 1 (Fact) or 2 (Rule).
+- Three big-endian u16 BYTE lengths: issuer, machine, fact; one u8 receipt
+  length; then big-endian u64 since and until. This fixed header is 29 bytes.
+- Payload order: issuer UTF-8, machine UTF-8, fact ASCII, receipt ASCII,
+  opaque 64-byte signature. No padding or trailing bytes; maximum 925 bytes.
+- Issuer/machine retain the core domain: 1..64 Unicode scalar values (at most
+  256 UTF-8 bytes each). They are opaque identifiers, not trusted instructions.
+  Fact is 1..256 bytes, each 0x20..0x7E; receipt is 1..64 ASCII alphanumeric
+  bytes or `-_.`; since < until. Wire u64 times are a narrower core i128 subset.
+- The signing prefix is the entire header and payload BEFORE the signature,
+  including issuer, every length and all six fields. Existing caller-supplied
+  verification accepts or refuses; this profile defines no signing algorithm.
+  Decode returns a borrowed verified view only after structural validation and
+  caller acceptance. Checked encoding also requires acceptance and leaves the
+  caller buffer unchanged on error; an unsigned prefix builder emits no frame.
+- These format, byte-order, time-width and strict-encoder choices are IMPOSED
+  experiment defaults, not adopted constants. Core-valid non-ASCII/control fact
+  text and times above u64::MAX are explicitly unencodable, never rewritten.
+  Receipt/replay/scope, interval application and conflict decisions remain in
+  the existing overlay policy. A verified frame alone grants no authority.
+- The heap-free crate has no default heap requirement; `alloc` adds owned core
+  conversion. Host simulation requires opt-in `rpp-link/sim`; its normal
+  default-features=false codec dependency preserves heap-free builds and makes
+  the simulation-feature visibility counterfactual a meaningful assertion test.
+
